Subject: [PATCH] gcc wrapper: apply the unaligned-vector-move workaround to AVX2

GCC on x86_64-w64-mingw32 emits 32/64-byte aligned vector moves against a stack
it only guarantees 16-byte alignment for, and it does not always insert a
realignment prologue, so those moves fault with STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION.

Upstream already passes -Wa,-muse-unaligned-vector-move for AVX-512 builds.
256-bit AVX2 code carries the identical defect: with GCC_ARCH=x86-64-v3, zimg's
GraphBuilder::impl::build_subgraph() spilled `vmovdqa %ymm0,0x70(%rsp)` from a
prologue that never realigned the stack, faulting on every mpv screenshot-raw
(which is how stremio-native generates timeline thumbnails).

Widening the gate from GCC_ARCH_HAS_AVX512 to GCC_ARCH_HAS_AVX covers both.
AVX-512 implies AVX, so this strictly subsumes the previous condition.

diff --git a/toolchain/gcc/gcc-compiler.in b/toolchain/gcc/gcc-compiler.in
index d4bc4d8..1a97d9e 100644
--- a/toolchain/gcc/gcc-compiler.in
+++ b/toolchain/gcc/gcc-compiler.in
@@ -10,7 +10,12 @@ else
     fi
 fi

-if [ "@GCC_ARCH_HAS_AVX512@" == "ON" ]; then
+# GCC on x86_64-w64-mingw32 emits 32/64-byte aligned vector moves against a
+# stack it only guarantees 16-byte alignment for, and it does not always insert
+# a realignment prologue, so those moves fault. Upstream applies this to AVX-512
+# only; 256-bit AVX2 code carries the identical defect, which crashed
+# zimg's GraphBuilder::impl::build_subgraph() on every mpv screenshot.
+if [ "@GCC_ARCH_HAS_AVX@" == "ON" ]; then
     FLAGS="$FLAGS -Wa,-muse-unaligned-vector-move"
 fi
